Syntax: mine

Mine cuts ore out of a rock face.  You need a pick in hand and hills,
mountains or a cave around you.  Sewers run deeper than any of them and hold
nothing worth having.

What the rock holds depends on where you are and how deep.  Hills give up
stone and the common metals; mountains hold iron, silver, gold and, deep
enough, the metals worth carrying home; caves are the only place crystal is
found, and below nine levels down that means gemstones.  Nothing is
impossible anywhere -- a hillside can hide a diamond -- it is only unlikely.

Every chunk cut is a chance the face gives out.  Near the surface that is
better than even odds; the deeper you are the longer a seam lasts, and at the
bottom of the world it is very nearly forever.

Metal ore goes to a crucible.  Stone and crystal wait for other hands.

See also: SMELT, FORGE, LUMBERJACK
